            "value": "SSH workspace"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "请根据我上传的参考图制作一个应用内角色头像。\n角色描述：[填写外貌、服饰、耳麦等特征]\n画风：[填写喜欢的画风]\n背景：[纯色或透明背景]\n输出一张 1:1 正方形图片，建议 1024×1024。脸部和上半身清晰，主体居中，头部占画面约 75%，保留头饰与耳麦的完整轮廓，四周留少量安全边距。小尺寸下也能辨认表情。保持参考角色身份，不添加文字、水印、边框或光效。": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Create an in-app character avatar from the reference image I uploaded.\nCharacter: [describe appearance, outfit, headset and other details]\nStyle: [preferred art style]\nBackground: [solid color or transparent]\nOutput one square 1:1 image, preferably 1024×1024. Show the face and upper body clearly, centered, with the head filling about 75% of the image. Preserve the full silhouette of the headwear and headset, with a small margin around the subject. Expressions must remain readable at small sizes. Preserve the reference character's identity. Do not add text, watermarks, borders or lighting effects."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "请以我上传的头像为唯一角色参考，制作一张用于循环思考动画的四帧动作图。\n输出一张 1:1 正方形图片，建议 1536×1536，严格按 2 列×2 行排成四个等大的正方形画面。没有外边距、格间距、分隔线、编号或文字。\n保持四帧中角色身份、画风、脸部比例、发色、头饰、服装、耳麦、背景和光照一致，镜头与头部位置、大小固定。\n阅读顺序为左上→右上→左下→右下：\n1. 眼睛睁开，视线略向上，手抬向下巴。\n2. 手指轻轻托住下巴，露出思索表情。\n3. 保持托腮姿势，轻轻闭眼眨眼。\n4. 睁眼，手开始放下，动作自然回到第一帧。\n动作与表情变化应在小头像里清晰可见。不要整体漂浮、旋转、缩放，不加光环、粒子或思考气泡，不改变角色造型。每帧内保留完整头饰与动作手部，背景与头像一致。[替换上面的动作描述也可以制作自己的循环动作。]": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Use my uploaded avatar as the only character reference to create a four-frame image for a looping thinking animation.\nOutput one square 1:1 image, preferably 1536×1536, divided into a strict 2×2 grid of equal square frames. No margins, gaps, separators, numbers or text.\nKeep identity, art style, facial proportions, hair, accessories, outfit, headset, background and lighting consistent. Keep the camera and head position and scale fixed.\nRead the frames from top left to top right, then bottom left to bottom right:\n1. Eyes open, looking slightly upward, hand lifting toward the chin.\n2. Fingers lightly supporting the chin, with a thoughtful expression.\n3. Keep the hand at the chin and close the eyes for a brief blink.\n4. Open the eyes and begin lowering the hand, returning naturally to frame one.\nMake pose changes readable in a small avatar. No overall floating, rotation or scaling; no halos, particles or thought bubbles; no character redesign. Keep all headwear and the acting hand visible in every frame. Match the avatar background. [Replace the pose descriptions to create your own animation loop.]"
          }
        }
      }
    },
